# A2UI: No Executable UI Across the Wire

## Context

Today `backend/utils/streaming.py` emits plain typed event dicts (`reasoning`,
`answer`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `agent`, `error`, `done`), and the
frontend renders them through fixed components — `StreamingRenderer.tsx` for
the event types, `MarkdownSection.tsx` (via `react-markdown` + `remark-gfm`)
for freeform agent text. That second piece matters: the frontend already
trusts agent-produced text enough to run it through a markdown renderer. A2UI
exists specifically to formalize and constrain that trust boundary — the
agent describes a component tree, the host renders it from a fixed, known
component set, and nothing the agent emits is ever interpreted as markup or
script.

## Hard rules

- Anything the agent sends toward rendering must be declarative A2UI
  component-tree JSON, validated against the A2UI schema before it reaches
  the frontend.
- The agent never emits raw HTML, embedded `<script>`, or
  markdown-with-executable-content that gets rendered without first going
  through the A2UI component contract.
- `MarkdownSection.tsx` either gets folded into the A2UI-rendered component
  set (as one allow-listed "markdown block" component type with sanitized
  rendering) or is retired — it does not survive as an unconstrained side
  channel that agent text can still reach.
- New A2UI component types get added deliberately, one at a time, to an
  explicit allow-list. No "just render whatever comes through" fallback.
